# pip-audit ignore list (WS-E.9, .github/workflows/ci.yml job `pip-audit`).
#
# Format: one advisory ID per line (e.g. GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx or
# PYSEC-xxxx-xxxx), nothing else on the line. Blank lines and lines
# starting with `#` are ignored. CI reads this file and passes each ID as
# `--ignore-vuln <ID>` to pip-audit.
#
# Every entry MUST have a comment block above it explaining: which
# package/advisory, why it's safe to skip right now (not exploitable in
# our usage, no fix released, etc.), and when to revisit. Do not add an
# entry just to make CI pass -- fix the dependency instead unless there is
# a real reason not to.

# ecdsa (transitive dependency of python-jose) -- pure-Python ECDSA
# signing/verification isn't constant-time (Minerva-class timing side
# channel). Upstream (tlsfuzzer/python-ecdsa) has stated this is a
# won't-fix: https://github.com/tlsfuzzer/python-ecdsa/issues/262. Not
# exploitable here -- JWT_ALGORITHM is hardcoded to HS256 everywhere in
# this codebase (core/config.py, core/security.py), so the ES*/ECDSA code
# path in python-jose/ecdsa is never executed. Revisit only if the JWT
# algorithm is ever changed to an ES* variant.
PYSEC-2026-1325
